let __v_5924 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"race\",\"Mass races start early and in waves: most city marathons and half marathons go off between 8 and 10 in the morning, a 10k usually between 9 and 10, and a parkrun at 9 on a Saturday. Your race email has your own wave and the time the pens close, which is the one people miss - and the earlier wave is often the one with the friendlier cut-offs.\"],[\"match\",\"Most Saturday football kicks off at 3pm and Sunday games at 2pm or 4.30pm, but a televised game moves by hours, so the club's or the ticket page's fixture list is the only reliable one. Turn up an hour before for a big ground, because the queues at the turnstiles are what make people late.\"],[\"gig\",\"Doors for a gig usually open an hour before the support act, and the headline act comes on about two hours after doors; most venues have a curfew at half past ten or eleven, so that is roughly when it ends. A big venue also has a bag check, so add twenty minutes. The venue's own page or your ticket email gives the door time, and check the last train home before the encore.\"],[\"fireworks\",\"A firework display goes up after dark, so most are between 7 and 9 in the evening in November and later in midsummer, and the organiser's page gives the exact time because it depends on sunset. Wrap up warm and stand upwind, and get there early if you are driving, since car parks empty slowly.\"]]}")?;
